claims:
1. A computer-implemented method for detecting capital allocation reversal failure signature in a subject entity, comprising:
    receiving, by a processor, quarterly financial filing data for the subject entity from a regulatory filing data source, wherein the quarterly financial filing data includes at least one of revenue trajectory, gross-margin trajectory, operating-expense trajectory, and capital-allocation trajectory;
    receiving, by the processor, counterparty network data for the subject entity, the counterparty network data being derived from a functional-network registry indicating supplier, customer, capital-provider, and regulator relationships of the subject entity;
    determining, by the processor, based at least in part on the quarterly financial filing data and the counterparty network data, a Orbitofrontal Cortex-equivalent decoupling score, wherein the determining the Orbitofrontal Cortex-equivalent decoupling score includes computing a phase-conditioned coupling factor from a peer cohort phase distribution;
    applying, by the processor, an inhibitory damping factor to the Orbitofrontal Cortex-equivalent decoupling score based at least in part on regulatory-edge counterparty signal, in response to determining that the regulatory-edge counterparty signal indicates an active oversight state;
    transmitting, by the processor, the Orbitofrontal Cortex-equivalent decoupling score to a portfolio risk system in response to determining that the score exceeds a predefined capital allocation reversal failure threshold.

1. A computer-implemented method for detecting executive comp misalignment signature in a subject entity, comprising:
    receiving, by a processor, quarterly financial filing data for the subject entity from a regulatory filing data source, wherein the quarterly financial filing data includes at least one of revenue trajectory, gross-margin trajectory, operating-expense trajectory, and capital-allocation trajectory;
    receiving, by the processor, counterparty network data for the subject entity, the counterparty network data being derived from a functional-network registry indicating supplier, customer, capital-provider, and regulator relationships of the subject entity;
    determining, by the processor, based at least in part on the quarterly financial filing data and the counterparty network data, a ventromedial Prefrontal Cortex-equivalent decoupling score, wherein the determining the ventromedial Prefrontal Cortex-equivalent decoupling score includes computing a phase-conditioned coupling factor from a peer cohort phase distribution;
    applying, by the processor, an inhibitory damping factor to the ventromedial Prefrontal Cortex-equivalent decoupling score based at least in part on regulatory-edge counterparty signal, in response to determining that the regulatory-edge counterparty signal indicates an active oversight state;
    transmitting, by the processor, the ventromedial Prefrontal Cortex-equivalent decoupling score to a portfolio risk system in response to determining that the score exceeds a predefined executive comp misalignment threshold.
